    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1950-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Increasing \\(r\\) by \\(100\\%\\) changes it to \\(2r.\\) The area changes from \\(\\pi r^2\\) to \\(\\pi(2r)^2=4\\pi r^2,\\) an increase of \\(3\\pi r^2.\\) This is \\(300\\%\\) of the original area.\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "An increase of \\(100\\%\\) doubles the radius",
        "Circle area is proportional to the square of the radius"
      ],
